<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yanji</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yanji is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jilin">Jilin province</a>, north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, and the capital of the Yanbian Korean Autonomous Prefecture, near the borders with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. The area lay in the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>, and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puxian-wannu">Puxian Wannu</a>'s Eastern Xia stood nearby in the early 13th century. From the late 19th century Korean settlement made it the main centre of China's Korean minority.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yanji.jpg" alt="Yanji" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: EditQ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%BB%B6%E5%90%89%E5%B8%82%E4%B8%AD%E5%BF%83.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
